{"schema_version": 2, "model": "google/gemini-3.8-flash", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 50000, "groups": 11}, "seed": 496559111, "solved": "failed", "parsed": true, "verify_ok": false, "verify_reason": "incompatible choices on constraint 3->8", "reply": "To find the valid values $(t_0, \\dots, t_{10}) \\in \\mathbb{P}^1(\\mathbb{F}_p)$ for $p = 50021$, we analyze the constraint graph. The graph contains a single cycle among groups $\\{3, 8, 10\\}$:\n- $t_8 = M_{3,8}(t_3)$ with $M_{3,8} = \\begin{pmatrix} 828 & 35534 \\\\ 36550 & 9745 \\end{pmatrix}$\n- $t_8 = M_{10,8}(t_{10})$ with $M_{10,8} = \\begin{pmatrix} 35438 & 19538 \\\\ 15884 & 597 \\end{pmatrix}$\n- $t_3 = M_{10,3}(t_{10})$ with $M_{10,3} = \\begin{pmatrix} 14371 & 10673 \\\\ 2157 & 7199 \\end{pmatrix}$\n\nThe holonomy matrix around the cycle acting on $t_{10}$ is given by:\n$$C = M_{10,8}^{-1} M_{3,8} M_{10,3}$$\n\n1. **Product $M_{3,8} M_{10,3} \\pmod{50021}$**:\n- $A_{11} = 828 \\cdot 14371 + 35534 \\cdot 2157 \\equiv 44211 + 14666 \\equiv 8856$\n- $A_{12} = 828 \\cdot 10673 + 35534 \\cdot 7199 \\equiv 39598 + 49058 \\equiv 38635$\n- $A_{21} = 36550 \\cdot 14371 + 9745 \\cdot 2157 \\equiv 46684 + 10424 \\equiv 7087$\n- $A_{22} = 36550 \\cdot 10673 + 9745 \\cdot 7199 \\equiv 21626 + 14300 \\equiv 35926$\n\n2. **Inverse $M_{10,8}^{-1}$**:\n$M_{10,8} = \\begin{pmatrix} 35438 & 19538 \\\\ 15884 & 597 \\end{pmatrix} \\implies M_{10,8}^{-1} \\propto \\begin{pmatrix} 597 & -19538 \\\\ -15884 & 35438 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 597 & 30483 \\\\ 34137 & 35438 \\end{pmatrix}$\n\n3. **Holonomy matrix $C = M_{10,8}^{-1} A \\pmod{50021}$**:\n- $C_{11} = 597 \\cdot 8856 + 30483 \\cdot 7087 \\equiv 28723 + 28833 \\equiv 7535$\n- $C_{12} = 597 \\cdot 38635 + 30483 \\cdot 35926 \\equiv 34799 + 45963 \\equiv 30741$\n- $C_{21} = 34137 \\cdot 8856 + 35438 \\cdot 7087 \\equiv 9425 + 26176 \\equiv 35601$\n- $C_{22} = 34137 \\cdot 38635 + 35438 \\cdot 35926 \\equiv 15998 + 43491 \\equiv 9468$\n\nSince the holonomy is parabolic, the fixed point equation $C(t) = t$, or $C_{21} t^2 + (C_{22} - C_{11})t - C_{12} = 0$, has a unique double root:\n$$t_{10} = \\frac{C_{11} - C_{22}}{2 C_{21}} = \\frac{7535 - 9468}{2 \\cdot 35601} = \\frac{-1933}{71202} \\equiv \\frac{48088}{21181} \\pmod{50021}$$\n$21181^{-1} \\pmod{50021} = 17951$\n$$t_{10} \\equiv 48088 \\cdot 17951 \\equiv 27552 \\pmod{50021}$$\n\n4. **Propagating values to all groups**:\n- $t_3 = M_{10,3}(t_{10}) = \\frac{14371 \\cdot 27552 + 10673}{2157 \\cdot 27552 + 7199} \\equiv 15615$\n- $t_0 = M_{3,0}(t_3) = \\frac{35933 \\cdot 15615 + 20898}{18421 \\cdot 15615 + 28389} \\equiv 28741$\n- $t_8 = M_{3,8}(t_3) = \\frac{828 \\cdot 15615 + 35534}{36550 \\cdot 15615 + 9745} \\equiv 43336$\n- $t_2 = M_{2,8}^{-1}(t_8) \\implies M_{2,8}(t_2) = t_8 \\implies t_2 \\equiv 22596$\n- $t_4 = M_{4,8}^{-1}(t_8) \\implies M_{4,8}(t_4) = t_8 \\implies t_4 \\equiv 31084$\n- $t_9 = M_{9,4}^{-1}(t_4) \\implies M_{9,4}(t_9) = t_4 \\implies t_9 \\equiv 11847$\n- $t_1 = M_{9,1}(t_9) = \\frac{46418 \\cdot 11847 + 13533}{2869 \\cdot 11847 + 19298} \\equiv 26038$\n- $t_6 = M_{6,4}^{-1}(t_4) \\implies M_{6,4}(t_6) = t_4 \\implies t_6 \\equiv 45914$\n- $t_7 = M_{7,6}^{-1}(t_6) \\implies M_{7,6}(t_7) = t_6 \\implies t_7 \\equiv 37042$\n- $t_5 = M_{7,5}(t_7) = \\frac{34524 \\cdot 37042 + 10765}{7520 \\cdot 37042 + 15831} \\equiv 9243$\n\n<answer>[[0,28741],[1,26038],[2,22596],[3,15615],[4,31084],[5,9243],[6,45914],[7,37042],[8,43336],[9,11847],[10,27552]]</answer>", "error": null, "elapsed_sec": 24.38, "http_status": 200, "finish_reason": "stop", "preset": "medium", "escalation_round": 0}
